  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The camera started to get really glitchy and choppy after the last update, which you rolled back last week.  That fixed the issue, but now you reimplemented the patch yesterday, and the camera is no longer locked to the head and moves very jerkily.  \n\nThe settings for the camera are \"Behavior>Look at me [ON]\" and \"Flying [ON]\"  Then move the flying camera in various directions with the thumbstuck.  You can see its very glitchy and jerkily moving now.  It never used to be like that.  It gets worse the more people are in the instance or the more draw on your system.  \n\nIt stopped working when last patch implemented, and the rollback fixed it.  Now that the patch is reimplemented, its bugged again.  \n\nThis is pretty obscure, but I use the in-game camera for all of my content, specifically this setting.  Please put it back to the way it was.",
